<spell-notebook "container theming">
	<header level="1">
		Container
		<header>A container limits content to a maximum width.</>
	</>
	<container-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-container-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or
			on the inner box through `::part(container)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each
			through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- The fixed widths are one token per breakpoint: `--ui-container-width-tablet`, `-computer`, `-large-monitor`.
			- The `scrolling` heights too: `--ui-container-scrolling-height` (phones, 15em), then
			  `--ui-container-scrolling-height-tablet` (18em), `-computer` (24em), `-widescreen` (30em).
			- Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every container on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-container-width-large-monitor: 1200px;
			}
			/* one article */
			article {
			  --ui-container-text-width: 640px;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-container" playground>
				<ui-container>
					<ui-text paragraph>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa strong. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.</>
					<ui-text paragraph>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa strong. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>A container has no look of its own:  the theme in the header changes the type inside it.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
